named_blocks.source_text:
Key equation — Taylor expansion with remainder For $f\in C^2$: $\ f(x+\delta)=f(x)+
abla f(x)^{	op}\delta+	frac12\delta^{	op}
abla^2f(x)\,\delta+o(\|\delta\|^2)$. If $\|
abla^2f\|\le M$ on the segment from $x$ to $x+\delta$, then $|f(x+\delta)-f(x)-
abla f(x)^{	op}\delta|\le	frac M2\|\delta\|^2$ (one-variable Taylor with remainder applied to $t\mapsto f(x+t\delta)$, whose second derivative is $\delta^{	op}
abla^2f\,\delta$).

